WEBVTT

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:04.970
I didn't know you could play the piano.

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:09.510
You're much softer than you were back then.

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:12.140
Whose fault is that I wonder?

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.480
Whose fault?

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:17.700
Kaho-chan...

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.040
Hihara-sempai, what's wrong?

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.330
Oh, I see...

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.080
I like her.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:08.100
The Lying Violin

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:21.860
Hihara, did something good happen?

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:23.500
Yeah. Actually, yesterday...

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:33.460
No, it's nothing.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.950
Anyway, I need to hurry.

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:38.540
I wonder what Kanayan wants to talk about in the middle of lunch break...

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:47.310
Music Room

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:47.310
A violin class?

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:52.490
Yeah, I sometimes do trial lessons at the city rec centers,

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:56.290
but the person I do it with is busy and can't come this time.

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:58.490
I thought I'd invite some people from the orchestra,

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:03.170
but Kanazawa-sensei suggested asking the people in the contest.

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:04.470
What do you think?

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:07.360
Sorry, today's not a good day.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:09.810
I'm kind of busy too.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:12.490
I'm sorry I can't help.

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:17.190
Um, I... I'm sorry.

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:19.890
No, don't worry about it.

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:22.130
I'm the one asking you.

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:28.270
Well, if I could make one request, I would like the two who play the violin to come.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:36.250
Come on, it'll be a good experience! Help him out.

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:40.590
Um, I don't really mind, but...

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:47.650
If you two would both like me to...

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:48.790
Thanks!

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:49.610
It's a huge help.

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:51.530
Sorry, Tsukimori.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:52.450
Don't mention it.

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:54.320
Sorry.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:57.070
OK, I'll go too!

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:58.920
So will I.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:02.710
I don't really have anything to do...

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:03.850
Thanks!

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:07.210
If you come with us, we can do a quartet.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.640
A quartet?

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:12.490
I will go.

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:13.900
Thanks.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:17.230
Quartet Quartet Quartet

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:17.230
Kanezawa-sensei, can I borrow a viola?

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:18.740
Sure.

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:21.140
You can play the viola, that's right.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:23.070
What about me?

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:25.820
We'll need somebody to help out with the kids and stuff.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.070
You're perfect for it.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:30.020
That's horrible, Kanayan!

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:32.700
There are a lot of kids, it would really help if you came.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:34.510
That's right.

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:37.810
Hihara would probably be able to become friends with them really quickly...

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.870
Yunoki... Osaki-sempai...

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:41.920
So basically you'd just help out.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.910
Stupid Kanayan.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:46.760
Now now, Hihara-sempai.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:49.260
Let's do our best, OK?

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:50.850
Y-Yeah.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.610
I'm looking forward to it, Kaho-chan.

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:59.920
OK, let's start the violin class.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:01.740
Nice to meet you everyone.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:03.190
Let's have some fun.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:11.350
Hi!

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:13.520
Nice to meet you.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:16.750
Um, hello...

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:22.650
OK, then let's start by playing a song...

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:27.010
A song played with four people like this is called a "quartet".

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:34.640
The song we're playing for you today is "Eine Kline Nachtmusik" by a man named Mozart.

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:38.080
No way!

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:39.990
I can't play that all of a sudden!

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:41.800
One Hour Earlier

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:41.810
I've never played it before...

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:44.050
You can just play the main melody, OK?

00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:44.860
Try your best.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:47.060
B-But...

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:52.450
I'll help out if you get in trouble.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.580
What?

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:59.540
I'll do my best too.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:02.680
Come on, please? Hino-san.

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:05.800
Th-There's nowhere for me to run?

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:08.350
Hino-san? Hino-san?

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:10.550
Are you OK?

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:11.540
We're starting.

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:13.220
Yes, I'm sorry.

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:15.440
OK, from the fifth beat...

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:20.690
Fifth beat...

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:25.890
We're off...

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:33.710
Geez, so I am stuck running errands.

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:37.030
I wonder if their performance is over.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:41.590
Kaho-chan...

00:06:57.410 --> 00:06:58.770
What should I do?

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:00.430
I can't keep up with them.

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:05.150
Hino... Hino?

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:07.060
Your tempo is too fast.

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:10.990
Follow my lead for the next four bars.

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:25.990
I'm still too fast... I need to slow down.

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:41.940
Amazing. We're in perfect harmony...

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:27.170
We were in perfect harmony for the last half, weren't we?

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:29.690
Yeah, it was great!

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:34.110
Um... want to do it again?

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:37.350
Tsukimori-kun?

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:40.470
Um, thanks.

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:43.000
How are you going to make it if you can't even play a song like that?

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.290
Try harder next time.

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:46.430
You're right.

00:08:46.430 --> 00:08:47.760
I'm really sorry.

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:52.100
What's wrong, Tsukimori-kun?

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:53.030
Nothing.

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:56.940
You're much more honest with yourself than usual.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:03.700
Tsukimori-kun... is he maybe softer than he was somehow?

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:07.130
Huh?

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:08.810
Is the performance over?

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:09.550
Yes.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:14.280
Too bad, I wanted to hear it!

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:16.910
No. It wasn't worth hearing.

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:24.380
Well, maybe he is...

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:27.380
Now, this is a serious responsibility!

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:31.250
For these things the intuition of a wild animal is what you should rely on.

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:36.260
You're going to decide the order for the third selection.

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:50.270
I guess I have to do it myself then after all...

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:56.940
OK, then put your hand on the strings, lightly, and keep your nose pointed at the end of the violin.

00:09:56.940 --> 00:09:58.280
That's right.

00:09:59.710 --> 00:10:06.290
Those kid violins are cute... I'm pretty sure they're called fractional size violins.

00:10:06.510 --> 00:10:07.880
Like this?

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:09.630
Yeah, that's right.

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:10.920
Like this?

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.460
Yeah, that's right.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:15.550
Hihara-sempai?

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:18.030
What are you doing?

00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:20.250
I thought I'd join in...

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:21.090
Is that not OK?

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:22.740
No, it's all right...

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:23.800
Great!

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:27.700
Hey, you're holding it weird.

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:30.310
Excuse me for a second.

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:34.120
You should point your arm this way, I think.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:38.070
Or was it like this?

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:43.290
Hihara-sempai?

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:44.500
I-I'm sorry!

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:45.780
It's nothing.

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:48.210
Um, don't you play it like this?

00:10:52.870 --> 00:10:53.810
Amazing!

00:10:53.810 --> 00:10:55.720
It actually made a sound!

00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:59.230
It's kind of mysterious!

00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:09.020
When holding the violin, make sure to hold the bow and bridge of the violin level, and play like so.

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:14.290
Any questions?

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:17.670
Yes! Yes! Yes!

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:21.350
Everybody's really into it.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:27.200
This is kinda fun.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:28.660
Everybody's having a great time.

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:32.930
Wow!

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:38.210
Yeah, they really look like they're having fun.

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:39.840
Kaho-chan?

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:45.040
I always wanted to play it...

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:52.690
Huh?

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:54.800
There's not enough violins.

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:57.640
I wonder if there's still some in the classroom.

00:11:57.640 --> 00:11:59.820
I'll go get them.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:00.990
Thanks.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:02.770
That's a huge help.

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:04.830
If you need help carrying them, let me know.

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:06.330
OK!

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:11.660
If I had started early...

00:12:12.380 --> 00:12:15.170
Well, no sense in thinking about it.

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:22.190
There they are.

00:12:22.190 --> 00:12:24.760
I can carry two on my own.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:27.230
Come to think of it...

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:31.230
I may never have really touched a normal violin.

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:39.010
Normal, huh?

00:13:01.350 --> 00:13:03.060
It sounds horrible.

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:06.730
Actually, my left hand isn't even keeping up.

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:24.070
I knew that.

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:25.050
Knew what?

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:32.550
What did you know?

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:57.950
What was that sound?

00:13:57.950 --> 00:14:00.520
Would you explain it to me, Hino?

00:14:00.970 --> 00:14:02.530
No way...

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:03.390
I'm sorry!

00:14:03.390 --> 00:14:04.580
Kaho-chan, I'll help you.

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:10.480
What's wrong, you two?

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:15.380
Kaho-chan!

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:18.010
Kaho-chan?

00:14:27.230 --> 00:14:29.930
To think that Tsukimori-kun would see me...

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:32.040
How can I fool him?

00:14:32.590 --> 00:14:35.420
Fool him?

00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:40.490
Lies... excuses... tricks...

00:14:41.490 --> 00:14:44.010
Every time something happens, I...

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:48.950
When did I become like this?

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:51.790
Miss!

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:53.990
Violin lady!

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:56.610
Thanks for today!

00:14:56.610 --> 00:14:58.640
It was really fun!

00:14:58.640 --> 00:14:59.710
Same for me!

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:02.390
Same for me!

00:15:02.390 --> 00:15:06.050
I'm going to practice a lot and be really good like you!

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:10.540
Will you come teach us again?

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:12.500
Will you?

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:15.550
Hey, everyone.

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:18.160
Do you hate liars?

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:19.930
Liars?

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:22.890
I do!

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:24.070
I do too!

00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:25.640
Lying is wrong!

00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:27.330
I don't like liars!

00:15:27.330 --> 00:15:28.460
Me too!

00:15:28.460 --> 00:15:29.710
Me too!

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:32.330
Yeah, that's right.

00:15:32.330 --> 00:15:33.900
You do, don't you?

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:42.420
Miss?

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:44.490
What's wrong?

00:15:44.490 --> 00:15:45.890
Does your stomach hurt?

00:15:45.890 --> 00:15:48.350
Miss...

00:15:48.350 --> 00:15:49.740
Are you OK?

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:50.620
Miss...

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:51.290
What's wrong?

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:54.010
Kaho-chan!

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:56.470
Oh geez...

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:57.830
The strawberry is cute!

00:15:57.830 --> 00:15:59.040
Perfect, perfect!

00:15:59.970 --> 00:16:03.300
Hey, Hihara-cchi, cheer up!

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:06.030
Bye-bye!

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:10.330
What's wrong, Hihara?

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:15.730
It'll get stuck that way.

00:16:15.730 --> 00:16:18.610
Ow!

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:21.920
So, what's wrong? You're really out of it.

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:23.450
Am I?

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:25.350
Don't "Am I" me.

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:29.480
By the way, how was Osaki-sempai's thing?

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:32.720
It was fun.

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:34.760
There were a lot of kids.

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:36.170
Hihara?

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:38.160
Did something happen?

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:40.900
No.

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:44.130
It's not that anything happened...

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:46.290
But I don't get it.

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:51.810
A lot of feelings just came pouring out of nowhere, and when I started thinking about things, my heart just...

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:55.190
It's all clouded.

00:17:12.540 --> 00:17:14.250
Hino...

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:17.760
Tsuchiura-kun...

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:19.970
Is something wrong?

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:30.900
Nothing's wrong.

00:17:33.340 --> 00:17:35.920
It doesn't look like it.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:38.370
Did something bad happen?

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:46.340
Is it something you can't tell me?

00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:49.070
No, that's not it...

00:17:51.490 --> 00:17:53.090
Hino...

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:58.890
I'm sorry, I'm going back to the classroom.

00:17:59.490 --> 00:18:01.440
Hey, Hino!

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:06.790
What happened with her?

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:08.390
Tsuchiura.

00:18:08.390 --> 00:18:09.370
What?

00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:13.680
Did you know Hino before the competition?

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:15.960
No.

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:19.400
I see.

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:22.430
Hey, did something happen with her?

00:18:22.430 --> 00:18:24.900
That thing just now was because you showed up...

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:27.000
No.

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:38.450
What happened? To both Hino and Tsukimori...

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:39.710
Tsuchiura?

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:42.540
Sasaki? Captain?

00:18:42.540 --> 00:18:44.800
You spending lunch practicing the piano too?

00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:46.930
Yeah, I guess.

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:49.020
Captain.

00:18:49.780 --> 00:18:50.800
What?

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:53.280
How are the district preliminaries looking?

00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:56.500
You don't need to worry about it.

00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:58.940
The third selection is coming up, right?

00:18:58.940 --> 00:19:00.330
Captain?

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:02.090
See you, Tsuchiura!

00:19:04.070 --> 00:19:05.830
Captain...

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:10.200
I see... you're practicing again today.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:10.950
Yeah.

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:13.850
You really are trying your best every day.

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:15.310
Good, good!

00:19:15.310 --> 00:19:16.140
Bye!

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:17.460
See you tomorrow.

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:21.810
"Good"?

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:24.790
But... I have to.

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:30.760
I have to play as much as I can, and get even a little bit better.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:35.480
If I don't want to lie, I have to become the real thing.

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:38.850
And if I can't, then I have to get as close as I can.

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:43.060
More precise... stronger...

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:46.910
More... more... more...

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:47.670
Hey.

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:51.760
Why are you forcing yourself?

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:53.590
The strings will break.

00:19:55.310 --> 00:19:57.300
Tsukimori-kun...

00:19:57.300 --> 00:19:58.720
I-I'm sorry.

00:19:58.720 --> 00:20:00.100
You want to use the practice room?

00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:01.660
I'll clean up right away.

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:02.690
Why are you running?

00:20:03.670 --> 00:20:07.470
I haven't heard an explanation about yesterday.

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:11.770
That was... I was just playing around with it.

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:14.690
I'm trying to trick him again...

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:17.470
But now that's all I can do.

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:20.570
That wasn't your usual sound.

00:20:21.350 --> 00:20:22.800
Well...

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:24.080
Why are you avoiding me?

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:24.740
Let me go.

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:28.270
It's because there's something about it that makes you feel guilty, isn't it?

00:20:28.270 --> 00:20:29.200
Let me go!

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:35.060
There's so much about you I don't understand.

00:20:35.060 --> 00:20:38.170
I've heard that you just started playing the violin,

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:41.000
but from hearing your performances, that doesn't seem to be the case.

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:46.230
And yet your musical knowledge is far too lacking for you to have played for years.

00:20:46.230 --> 00:20:49.170
And then to top it off, your playing yesterday.

00:20:49.170 --> 00:20:52.970
Hino, you were playing that seriously, weren't you?

00:20:53.370 --> 00:21:01.400
It's all a mystery... it's almost as if you can only play that violin.

00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:12.700
That's impossible...

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:13.830
I agree.

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:19.290
And what's more, no matter what secret it holds, that doesn't matter to me.

00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:27.840
What matters to me is your feelings as you participate in this contest... your attitude toward music.

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:30.380
Well, Hino?

00:21:36.930 --> 00:21:42.840
Which means... that I cannot accept you.

00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:56.130
I have nothing...

00:21:57.180 --> 00:22:03.450
I have nothing to contradict what he said.

00:23:36.620 --> 00:23:39.780
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:39.780 --> 00:23:43.860
The genius Mozart traveled Europe ever since he was a child,

00:23:43.860 --> 00:23:47.870
playing hugely successful performances for imperial courts and public concerts.

00:23:47.870 --> 00:23:49.300
When he was six, he traveled to

00:23:49.300 --> 00:23:51.650
Vienna with his father and older sister,

00:23:51.650 --> 00:23:54.100
where he was invited to Schonbrunn palace, where he received a standing ovation

00:23:54.100 --> 00:23:56.330
as he performed before empress Maria Theresia.

00:23:56.330 --> 00:23:58.190
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:23:58.190 --> 00:24:03.200
There's a story that says at the time he proposed to a seven year old girl during his time there.

00:24:03.200 --> 00:24:05.130
Who did that person later become?

00:24:06.240 --> 00:24:07.900
The third selection is almost here.

00:24:07.900 --> 00:24:09.810
But at this rate I can't play.

00:24:09.810 --> 00:24:12.920
What's wrong? You can talk to me about it if you want.

00:24:12.920 --> 00:24:15.220
You're a counselor too?

00:24:15.920 --> 00:24:18.100
Next episode: Crescendo of Uneasiness.

00:24:18.100 --> 00:24:20.090
Is it wrong if I just like it?

00:24:20.570 --> 00:24:25.090
The answer is... Marie Antoinette!

00:24:22.080 --> 00:24:25.090
Let them eat cake!
